WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.240
You asked AI to help with your project. You got a wall of text that builds into nothing.

2
00:00:06.690 --> 00:00:11.970
It is not the model. We give commands, when an agent needs delegation.

3
00:00:12.420 --> 00:00:18.180
Software one point oh — we wrote every line. Two point oh — machines learned from data.

4
00:00:18.630 --> 00:00:25.750
Three point oh — the agent writes the code. Your work is framing, context, and verification.

5
00:00:26.200 --> 00:00:31.080
Framing the task is the core skill. One meeting is devoted to it.

6
00:00:31.530 --> 00:00:37.210
Context and memory: without them the agent forgets everything in five minutes.

7
00:00:37.660 --> 00:00:41.420
The working environment you live in with your agent every day.

8
00:00:41.870 --> 00:00:47.390
Extension tools: from Claude Code user to architect of your own system.

9
00:00:47.840 --> 00:00:53.520
Eight meetings. Not lectures — each ends with an experiment on your own machine.

10
00:00:53.970 --> 00:00:58.450
New to AI coding? There is a kickstart that lowers the load at the start.

11
00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:02.900
You leave with a working system of your own, not with notes.

12
00:01:03.350 --> 00:01:07.270
Tochka sborki. Start with the first lesson.
